From 873121ed6b46fbbc019bf99abf88138cc77631dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 18:11:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] core/qt/android: opt-in report of installed and played games
 to the custom server

New setting "Share my installed and played games with the server" (share_games_with_server,
off by default; Configure > General > Network under Nintendo services, enabled only with a
custom server; Android: config.ini [WebService]). When on and the custom Nintendo server is set,
every game start (System::Load, so also games started from the HOME Menu) sends, from a
background thread so the game never waits for it:

  POST <custom server>/tangelo/v1/games   X-Tangelo-Original-Host: tangelo
  {"console_id": "<CFG Console ID>", "started": "<title ID>", "installed": [...],
   "tangelo": "<version>", "platform": "windows|android|linux|macos"}

Installed = games, demos, updates and DLC (title ID high 00040000/00040002/0004000E/0004008C)
with a content folder on the virtual SD card or in the NAND. The Console ID is per install; the
server links it to the friends account that signs in from the same address. Nothing is sent to
Nintendo, and nothing at all with the setting off.

Tests: report body and server address handling (2 new cases, 113 passed); the title scan was
checked against a fake SD/NAND (game, demo, update and DLC found; system title and a folder
without content skipped). Qt settings page and config compile; core.cpp and tangelo_report.cpp
compile for aarch64 (libc++).

